IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g4-interpretation`
IMPORT `g4-nouns`
IMPORT `g4-art11-application`
IMPORT `g4-art11-decision`
IMPORT `g4-art12-name`
IMPORT `ind-a-tests-fixtures`

-- ind-a-tests-art11-12.l4: independent tests of Articles 11 and 12 (the application, the decision, the name).
-- Expected values from WORK/ind-a/expectations.md (S11.x, S12.x). The Commissioner's satisfaction and opinions are supplied as stated inputs.

§ `ind-a tests: Articles 11 and 12`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN twelve IS A `How the twelve months preceding an application are counted`
      feb29 IS A `How a year is taken back from 29 February`
      noncomply IS A `What an application that does not comply leads to`
GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12`
`ind-a K with` twelve feb29 noncomply MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` WITH
        `how the twelve months preceding the application are counted` IS twelve
        `which day is the date of the application` IS `the day the application is lodged`
        `what an application that does not comply leads to` IS noncomply
        `how the duty to register meets the bars on granting the application` IS `a bar on granting the application displaces the duty to register`
        `whether a formerly registered charity is another registered charity` IS `a formerly registered charity is not another registered charity`
        `how a year is taken back from 29 February` IS feb29
        `which names of another registered charity Article 12(1)(a) compares` IS `its registered name and its alternative registered names`
        `whether a previous registered name is still one of its registered names` IS `a previous registered name is not one of its registered names`
        `how the period for the Commissioner's decision is counted` IS `the period starts the day after the date of the application`
        `how reasonable time and as soon as practicable are read for the guidance` IS `as a determination the caller supplies`
        `which payees Article 11(2)(e)(ii) reaches` IS `a payee who was a governor when the payment was made`
        `how applies or should be applied is read in Article 11(4)(f)` IS `a ground of mandatory refusal applies, or a ground of discretionary refusal should be applied`

-- My reading P1 (the day before the application ends the window, the same date a year earlier begins it, 28 February for 29 February).
`ind-a K` MEANS `ind-a K with` `the twelve months ending on the day before the application` `a year before 29 February is 28 February` `no duty to register or to refuse arises while the application does not comply`
-- The alternative P2 (the window ends on the application day).
`ind-a K P2` MEANS `ind-a K with` `the twelve months ending on the day of the application` `a year before 29 February is 28 February` `no duty to register or to refuse arises while the application does not comply`
-- The rolling 29 February.
`ind-a K roll` MEANS `ind-a K with` `the twelve months ending on the day before the application` `a year before 29 February is 1 March` `no duty to register or to refuse arises while the application does not comply`
-- The other reading of AMBIG-11: a non-complying application must be refused.
`ind-a K must refuse non-compliant` MEANS `ind-a K with` `the twelve months ending on the day before the application` `a year before 29 February is 28 February` `the Commissioner must refuse an application that does not comply`

`ind-a info given` MEANS `Information on a matter under Article 11(2)(a)` WITH `provided as at the time of the application` IS TRUE, `would differ once the entity is registered` IS FALSE, `provided as proposed once the entity is registered` IS FALSE

GIVEN lodged IS A DATE
      constitution IS A BOOLEAN
      draftPurposes IS A BOOLEAN
      draftPBS IS A BOOLEAN
      accountsExist IS A BOOLEAN
      restricted IS A BOOLEAN
      orderFurther IS A BOOLEAN
      furtherGiven IS A BOOLEAN
      payments IS A LIST OF `Payment to a governor`
      disclosed IS A LIST OF `Payment to a governor`
GIVETH AN `Application for registration`
`ind-a application` lodged constitution draftPurposes draftPBS accountsExist restricted orderFurther furtherGiven payments disclosed MEANS
    `Application for registration` WITH
        dates IS `Dates of an application` WITH `date lodged` IS lodged, `date on which it became complete` IS JUST lodged
        `particulars under Article 11(2)(a)` IS `Particulars under Article 11(2)(a)` WITH
            `how the applicant meets Article 11(4)(c) and (d)` IS `ind-a info given`
            `matters under Article 8(3)(a), (b) and (d)` IS `ind-a info given`
            `matters under Article 8(3)(h), (i), (m) and (n) apply to the applicant` IS FALSE
            `matters under Article 8(3)(h), (i), (m) and (n)` IS `ind-a info given`
        `documents under Article 11(2)(b) to (d)` IS `Documents under Article 11(2)(b) to (d)` WITH
            `copy of the applicant's constitution` IS constitution
            `draft of the proposed statement of registered charitable purposes` IS draftPurposes
            `draft of the registered public benefit statement` IS draftPBS
        `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)` IS `Financial details under Article 11(2)(e)` WITH
            `most recent financial accounts exist` IS accountsExist
            `details of the most recent financial accounts` IS FALSE
            `payments made to governors` IS payments
            `payments to governors disclosed in the application` IS disclosed
            `draft of the proposed statement under an Order under Article 13(9)(b)` IS FALSE
            `Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008 would require other financial information` IS FALSE
            `other financial information required under that Law` IS FALSE
            `entry in the restricted section is requested` IS restricted
            `Order prescribes further financial information` IS orderFurther
            `further financial information prescribed by Order` IS furtherGiven
        `other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)` IS `Other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)` WITH
            `Regulations under Article 11(3) require other information, documents or evidence` IS FALSE
            `other information, documents and evidence required by Regulations` IS FALSE
            `procedure under Regulations under Article 11(3)(b) followed` IS TRUE
            `Commissioner has requested other information, documents or evidence to determine the application` IS FALSE
            `other information, documents and evidence requested by the Commissioner` IS FALSE
        `provisions of Article 11(2) that an Order disapplies for this applicant` IS EMPTY

-- A complete application lodged on 15 March 2025, no accounts yet, no payments.
`ind-a complete application` MEANS `ind-a application` (YMD 2025 3 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY EMPTY

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Application for registration`
`ind-a application lodged on` d MEANS `ind-a application` d TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY EMPTY

GIVEN k IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12`
      app IS A DATE
      paid IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-a in window` k app paid MEANS `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` k (`ind-a application lodged on` app) paid

GIVEN k IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12`
      app IS AN `Application for registration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-a includes` k app MEANS `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` k app FALSE

GIVEN willMeet IS A BOOLEAN, written IS A BOOLEAN, carries IS A BOOLEAN, substantial IS A BOOLEAN, mustGround IS A BOOLEAN, mayPresent IS A BOOLEAN, mayApplied IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)`
`ind-a findings` willMeet written carries substantial mustGround mayPresent mayApplied MEANS
    `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)` WITH
        `applicant will meet the charity test on registration` IS willMeet
        `constitution of the applicant is a written document` IS written
        `applicant carries out, or intends to carry out, an activity in or from within Jersey` IS carries
        `activity is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial` IS substantial
        `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application must be refused applies` IS mustGround
        `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application may be refused has its circumstances present` IS mayPresent
        `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application may be refused should be applied` IS mayApplied

`ind-a good findings` MEANS `ind-a findings` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN jersey IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Entity
`ind-a applicant` jersey MEANS `ind-a entity` "Hope Jersey" `an applicant for registration` (LIST `a company`) jersey (LIST `ind-a Jersey resident individual`) (LIST `ind-a relief of poverty purpose`)

-- The Commissioner's duty on an application, with every bar off, on the readings given.
GIVEN k IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12`
      app IS AN `Application for registration`
      c195 IS A BOOLEAN
      jersey IS A BOOLEAN
      test IS A BOOLEAN
      findings IS A `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)`
      address IS A BOOLEAN
      undesirable IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Duty of the Commissioner on an application for registration`
`ind-a duty` k app c195 jersey test findings address undesirable MEANS
    `Art 11 the duty of the Commissioner on the application` k app FALSE c195 (`ind-a applicant` jersey) test findings address undesirable FALSE FALSE

`ind-a register` MEANS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
`ind-a refuse` MEANS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`

§§ `Article 11(2) (S11.2-01 to S11.2-12)`

-- S11.2-01 every item provided -> 11(2) complied (src:300-315)
#ASSERT `ind-a includes` `ind-a K` `ind-a complete application`
-- S11.2-02 missing constitution, draft purposes, draft PBS -> not complied (src:305-307)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a includes` `ind-a K` (`ind-a application` (YMD 2025 3 15) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a includes` `ind-a K` (`ind-a application` (YMD 2025 3 15) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a includes` `ind-a K` (`ind-a application` (YMD 2025 3 15) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY EMPTY)
-- S11.2-03 no accounts exist -> (e)(i) met (src:309)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(e)(i) the requirement is met` `ind-a complete application`
-- S11.2-04 an Order prescribes further financial information, not given: met if restricted entry is requested, not met otherwise (src:312)
#ASSERT `ind-a includes` `ind-a K` (`ind-a application` (YMD 2025 3 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EMPTY EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a includes` `ind-a K` (`ind-a application` (YMD 2025 3 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EMPTY EMPTY)
-- S11.2-05 (a)(iii) not applicable -> nothing needed (src:304)
#ASSERT `Art 11(2)(a)(iii) the requirement is met` `ind-a complete application`
-- S11.2-06 application 2025-03-15: a payment on 2024-03-14 is outside on both readings
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a in window` `ind-a K` (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2024 3 14)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a in window` `ind-a K P2` (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2024 3 14)
-- S11.2-07 a payment on 2024-03-15: inside on P1, outside on P2
#ASSERT `ind-a in window` `ind-a K` (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2024 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a in window` `ind-a K P2` (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2024 3 15)
-- S11.2-08 2024-03-16 and 2025-03-14: inside on both
#ASSERT `ind-a in window` `ind-a K` (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2024 3 16)
#ASSERT `ind-a in window` `ind-a K P2` (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2024 3 16)
#ASSERT `ind-a in window` `ind-a K` (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2025 3 14)
#ASSERT `ind-a in window` `ind-a K P2` (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2025 3 14)
-- S11.2-09 the application day itself: outside on P1, inside on P2
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a in window` `ind-a K` (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2025 3 15)
#ASSERT `ind-a in window` `ind-a K P2` (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2025 3 15)
-- S11.2-10 the day after: outside on both
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a in window` `ind-a K` (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2025 3 16)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a in window` `ind-a K P2` (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2025 3 16)
-- S11.2-11 application 2024-02-29: 2023-02-28 inside (clip), outside (roll); 2023-03-01 inside on both
#ASSERT `ind-a in window` `ind-a K` (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2023 2 28)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a in window` `ind-a K roll` (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2023 2 28)
#ASSERT `ind-a in window` `ind-a K` (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2023 3 1)
#ASSERT `ind-a in window` `ind-a K roll` (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2023 3 1)
-- S11.2-12 application 2025-02-28: a payment on 2024-02-29 is inside
#ASSERT `ind-a in window` `ind-a K` (YMD 2025 2 28) (YMD 2024 2 29)

`ind-a payment 2024-06-01` MEANS `Payment to a governor` WITH `name of the payee` IS "Ann Le Brun", `date of the payment` IS YMD 2024 6 1, `amount paid` IS 500, `payee was a governor when the payment was made` IS TRUE, `payee is a governor on the date of the application` IS TRUE

-- S11.2 a payment to a governor inside the window must be disclosed: undisclosed -> not complied; disclosed -> complied (src:310)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a includes` `ind-a K` (`ind-a application` (YMD 2025 3 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (LIST `ind-a payment 2024-06-01`) EMPTY)
#ASSERT `ind-a includes` `ind-a K` (`ind-a application` (YMD 2025 3 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (LIST `ind-a payment 2024-06-01`) (LIST `ind-a payment 2024-06-01`))

§§ `Article 11(4) and (5) (S11.4-00 to S11.5-01)`

-- S11.4-00 complies, satisfied of (a) to (f) -> must register (src:319-327)
#ASSERT `ind-a duty` `ind-a K` `ind-a complete application` TRUE TRUE TRUE `ind-a good findings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ind-a register`
-- S11.4-a1 fails the charity test and will not on registration -> must refuse (src:320, src:328)
#ASSERT `ind-a duty` `ind-a K` `ind-a complete application` TRUE TRUE FALSE `ind-a good findings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ind-a refuse`
-- S11.4-a2 will meet the test on registration -> (a) satisfied -> must register (src:320)
#ASSERT `ind-a duty` `ind-a K` `ind-a complete application` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`ind-a findings` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ind-a register`
-- S11.4-b1 unwritten constitution -> must refuse (src:321)
#ASSERT `ind-a duty` `ind-a K` `ind-a complete application` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`ind-a findings` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ind-a refuse`
-- S11.4-c1 a Jersey entity with no substantial activity -> must register (src:323)
#ASSERT `ind-a duty` `ind-a K` `ind-a complete application` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`ind-a findings` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ind-a register`
-- S11.4-c2, S11.4-c3 not a Jersey entity, carries out or intends a substantial activity in or from Jersey -> must register (src:324)
#ASSERT `ind-a duty` `ind-a K` `ind-a complete application` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`ind-a findings` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ind-a register`
-- S11.4-c4 not a Jersey entity, nothing substantial -> must refuse (src:322-324)
#ASSERT `ind-a duty` `ind-a K` `ind-a complete application` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`ind-a findings` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ind-a refuse`
-- S11.4-d1 no principal address in Jersey -> must refuse (src:325)
#ASSERT `ind-a duty` `ind-a K` `ind-a complete application` TRUE TRUE TRUE `ind-a good findings` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ind-a refuse`
-- S11.4-e1 undesirable name -> must refuse (src:326)
#ASSERT `ind-a duty` `ind-a K` `ind-a complete application` TRUE TRUE TRUE `ind-a good findings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ind-a refuse`
-- S11.4-f1 a mandatory prescribed ground -> refuse; a discretionary ground the Commissioner applies -> refuse; one he does not apply -> register (src:327)
#ASSERT `ind-a duty` `ind-a K` `ind-a complete application` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`ind-a findings` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ind-a refuse`
#ASSERT `ind-a duty` `ind-a K` `ind-a complete application` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`ind-a findings` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ind-a refuse`
#ASSERT `ind-a duty` `ind-a K` `ind-a complete application` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`ind-a findings` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ind-a register`
-- S11.4-p1 the 19(5) statement missing -> no duty to register (both readings of AMBIG-11 agree on that)
#ASSERT NOT (`ind-a duty` `ind-a K` `ind-a complete application` FALSE TRUE TRUE `ind-a good findings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ind-a register`)
#ASSERT NOT (`ind-a duty` `ind-a K must refuse non-compliant` `ind-a complete application` FALSE TRUE TRUE `ind-a good findings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ind-a register`)
-- S11.4-p1 AMBIG-11: reading "no decision owed" -> no duty either way; reading "must refuse" -> refuse
#ASSERT `ind-a duty` `ind-a K` `ind-a complete application` FALSE TRUE TRUE `ind-a good findings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`
#ASSERT `ind-a duty` `ind-a K must refuse non-compliant` `ind-a complete application` FALSE TRUE TRUE `ind-a good findings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ind-a refuse`
-- S11.4-p1 11(2) not complied (no constitution copy) -> no duty to register
#ASSERT NOT (`ind-a duty` `ind-a K` (`ind-a application` (YMD 2025 3 15) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY EMPTY) TRUE TRUE TRUE `ind-a good findings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ind-a register`)

§§ `Article 11(6) to (11) (S11.6-01 to S11.11-01)`

-- S11.6-01 5(6) applies to the substantiality guidance: issuing it without consulting the Minister is a breach (src:331, src:161)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(6)(b) the consultation and the report are as Article 5(6) requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 11(6)(b) the consultation and the report are as Article 5(6) requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- S11.6-01 the tribunal and the court must have regard (11(6)(d)); the Commissioner has its own duty in (c)
#ASSERT `Art 11(6)(d) the paragraph binds the party` `the court`
#ASSERT `Art 11(6)(d) the paragraph binds the party` `the Charity Tribunal`
#ASSERT `Art 11(6)(d) the paragraph binds the party` `a registered charity`
#ASSERT `Art 11(6)(d) the paragraph binds the party` `a governor`
-- S11.7-01 the example ground of 11(7)(a): only one governor, not carrying on a prescribed business as governor (src:335)
#ASSERT `Art 11(7)(a) the entity has only one governor who does not carry on a prescribed description of business as a governor` (`ind-a applicant` TRUE) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(7)(a) the entity has only one governor who does not carry on a prescribed description of business as a governor` (`ind-a applicant` TRUE) TRUE
-- S11.8-02, S11.8-03 an 11(8)(b) Order needs prior consultation of the Commissioner AND a representative body (src:341)
#ASSERT `Art 11(8)(b) the Minister has consulted as the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(8)(b) the Minister has consulted as the paragraph requires` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 11(8)(b) the Minister has consulted as the paragraph requires` TRUE FALSE

`ind-a registered Hope` MEANS
    `Registered charity` WITH
        entity IS `ind-a entity` "Hope Jersey" `entered in the general section` (LIST `a company`) TRUE (LIST `ind-a Jersey resident individual`) (LIST `ind-a relief of poverty purpose`)
        `registration number` IS "JC-0042"
        `registered name` IS "Hope Jersey"
        `alternative registered names` IS LIST "Hope"
        `date registered` IS YMD 2025 5 1
        `date deregistered` IS NOTHING
        `registered charitable purposes` IS LIST "the prevention or relief of poverty"
        `registered public benefit statement` IS "relief of poverty in Jersey by a food bank"
        `is an organized religious charity` IS FALSE

-- S11.9-01 on registering, a certificate with name, number and date discharges the duty; one with another name does not (src:345)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(9)(a) the Commissioner must issue a certificate of registration` TRUE `ind-a registered Hope` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, (`issue a certificate of registration` "Hope Jersey" "JC-0042" (YMD 2025 5 1))) AT 1
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(9)(a) the Commissioner must issue a certificate of registration` TRUE `ind-a registered Hope` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, (`issue a certificate of registration` "Hope" "JC-0042" (YMD 2025 5 1))) AT 1
-- S11.9-02 on entering a new or alternative name, a further certificate (src:346)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(9)(b) the Commissioner must issue a further certificate for a new or alternative registered name` TRUE "Hope" (YMD 2026 1 5) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, (`issue a further certificate for a new or alternative registered name` "Hope" (YMD 2026 1 5))) AT 1
-- S11.10-01 an applicant required to be NPO-registered but not: both duties stand until done (src:347-349)
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(10) the applicant must provide the additional information and request to be registered under that Law` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an applicant for registration` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `an applicant for registration`, `provide with the application the additional information that must be provided to the JFSC`) AT 1
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(10) the applicant must provide the additional information and request to be registered under that Law` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an applicant for registration` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `an applicant for registration`, `provide with the application the additional information that must be provided to the JFSC`) AT 1
    PARTY `an applicant for registration` DOES (`Act under Article 11` OF `an applicant for registration`, `request to be registered under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008`) AT 2
-- S11.10-02 not required (or already NPO-registered) -> no duty
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(10) the applicant must provide the additional information and request to be registered under that Law` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)
-- S11.11-01 the Commissioner received the request: must pass it to the JFSC; nothing received -> no duty (src:350-352)
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(11)(a) the Commissioner must pass the request to the JFSC` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 11(11)(a) the Commissioner must pass the request to the JFSC` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 11(11)(b) the JFSC must treat the request as an application for registration under that Law` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)

§§ `Article 12 (S12.1-01 to S12.7-06)`

GIVEN nm IS A STRING, kind IS A `Kind of entry of a name in the register`, st IS A `Standing on the register`, own IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Name entered in the register`
`ind-a entry` nm kind st own MEANS `Name entered in the register` WITH name IS nm, `kind of entry` IS kind, `standing of the entity that holds it` IS st, `held by the entity itself` IS own

GIVEN entries IS A LIST OF `Name entered in the register`
      mislead IS A BOOLEAN
      connected IS A BOOLEAN
      offensive IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name`
`ind-a opinion` entries mislead connected offensive MEANS
    `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` WITH
        `name in question` IS "Jersey Hope"
        `entries in the register that are the same as, or too similar to, the name` IS entries
        `likely to mislead the public as to the purpose, activities or identity of the entity` IS mislead
        `gives the impression that the entity is connected to a person to which it is not connected` IS connected
        `offensive` IS offensive

GIVEN o IS A `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-a undesirable` o MEANS `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` `ind-a K` o

-- S12.1-01, S12.1-02 the same as, or too similar to, another registered charity's name (src:355)
#ASSERT `ind-a undesirable` (`ind-a opinion` (LIST `ind-a entry` "Jersey Hope" `the registered name` `entered in the general section` FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `ind-a undesirable` (`ind-a opinion` (LIST `ind-a entry` "Jersey Hope Trust" `the registered name` `entered in the restricted section` FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- S12.1-03 the same as a deregistered charity's former name, nothing else -> not undesirable under (a) (src:355)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a undesirable` (`ind-a opinion` (LIST `ind-a entry` "Jersey Hope" `the registered name` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section` FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- S12.1-04 to S12.1-06 misleading; false connection; offensive -> undesirable (src:356-358)
#ASSERT `ind-a undesirable` (`ind-a opinion` EMPTY TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `ind-a undesirable` (`ind-a opinion` EMPTY FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `ind-a undesirable` (`ind-a opinion` EMPTY FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- S12.1-07 none -> not undesirable (src:354)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a undesirable` (`ind-a opinion` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- S12.2-01 on registering: the name entered as the registered name (src:360)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(2)(a) the Commissioner must enter the name of the entity in the register as the registered name` (`ind-a applicant` TRUE) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `the Commissioner`, (`enter the name of the entity in the register as the registered name` "Hope Jersey")) AT 1
-- S12.2-01 and a number allocated and entered (src:361)
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 12(2) the Commissioner must enter the registered name and allocate and enter a number` (`ind-a applicant` TRUE) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES (`Act under Article 12` OF `the Commissioner`, (`enter the name of the entity in the register as the registered name` "Hope Jersey")) AT 1
-- S12.4-01 a ground applies to the proposed name -> must refuse (src:363)
#ASSERT `Art 12(4) what the Commissioner must do on the application for permission` TRUE EQUALS JUST (`Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to permit a change or addition of registered name, Article 12(4)`, `the Commissioner refuses`)
-- S12.4-02 no ground -> no obligation either way (my reading: the Commissioner may grant)
#ASSERT `Art 12(4) what the Commissioner must do on the application for permission` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- S12.5-01 permission granted and change notified -> must enter the new name (src:364)
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 12(5) the Commissioner must enter the new or alternative registered name` TRUE "Hope" `the addition of an alternative registered name` TRUE "Hope" `the addition of an alternative registered name` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 60)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 12(5) the Commissioner must enter the new or alternative registered name` TRUE "Hope" `the addition of an alternative registered name` TRUE "Hope" `the addition of an alternative registered name` AT 0 WITH
